## What's the problem

The hadolint pin in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `.config/hadolint/Dockerfile` uses the `docker.io/` registry prefix (`docker.io/hadolint/hadolint:latest@sha256:...`). Dependabot cannot parse `docker.io/` or `ghcr.io/` prefixed container image references — it only handles the bare image name format (`hadolint/hadolint:latest@sha256:...`).

The prior slice (#4253) changed from `ghcr.io` → `docker.io`, which was incorrect.

## What it impacts

- Dependabot now tracks the hadolint Docker image for security updates via the `docker` ecosystem entry already in `dependabot.yml`
- CI hadolint step and the Dockerfile build remain functionally unchanged

## How I found it

Dependabot PRs for the hadolint `docker://` pins are never opened. The pinned reference includes a registry domain (`docker.io/`) which Dependabot's docker parser rejects. The fix is the bare image reference.

## How important is it

High — without this fix Dependabot never creates update PRs for the hadolint image, leaving the CI Dockerfile lint tool unpatched for CVEs.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] `.github/workflows/ci.yml` uses `hadolint/hadolint:latest@sha256:...` (no registry prefix)
- [x] `.config/hadolint/Dockerfile` uses `hadolint/hadolint:latest@sha256:...` (no registry prefix)
- [x] Dependabot's `docker` ecosystem entry in `.github/dependabot.yml` will now match and create update PRs

## Possible solutions

One change per file: strip the `docker.io/` prefix from the image reference. This is the only format Dependabot's docker parser accepts.

